**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Will not takes an infinitive without to.","B":"The verb after will not must remain base form.","C":"**Won’t** expands to **will not**; keep the base verb unchanged.","D":"Would not changes the modal and meaning; it does not expand won’t."}}},{"id":"ce527fd8-5091-5955-acf7-f0d1b7af7791","topicSlug":"register-variation","level":"C1","prompt":"Choose a standard polite modal request asking someone to restore the old portrait.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Do could you restore the old portrait, please?"},{"id":"B","text":"Could you restore the old portrait, please?"},{"id":"C","text":"Could you to restore the old portrait, please?"},{"id":"D","text":"Could you restored the old portrait, please?"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"Use the **modal question** pattern to make a polite request.","explanation":"**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request.","keywords":["polite-request-register"],"skill":"polite-request-register","contextKey":"register-variation-2","fingerprint":"acf0182fabe43b81d2967921e27afd4f3e93e1940d3bed16eab3fb00eb384453","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-varieties"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Use the **modal question** pattern to make a polite request.","**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request.","Choose **Could you restore the old portrait, please?**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Could forms its own question; do-support is not added.","B":"**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request.","C":"Could takes a bare infinitive without to.","D":"The main verb after could remains base, not past."}}},{"id":"2995652f-3cc6-5b16-a372-dabc68f6b8d3","topicSlug":"register-variation","level":"C1","prompt":"Expand “she’s” in “She’s measuring the garden fence right now.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"she is"},{"id":"B","text":"she has"},{"id":"C","text":"she was"},{"id":"D","text":"she does"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"Use the following **-ing form** to identify the auxiliary.","explanation":"Before the active -ing form **measuring**, she’s expands to **she is**.","keywords":["expand-progressive-contraction"],"skill":"expand-progressive-contraction","contextKey":"register-variation-3","fingerprint":"9a25cea5665986b9cac2d0daca277332820a47b1321fd587fa6759329ddf7ee4","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-varieties"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Use the following **-ing form** to identify the auxiliary.","Before the active -ing form **measuring**, she’s expands to **she is**.","Choose **she is**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Before the active -ing form **measuring**, she’s expands to **she is**.","B":"Has alone cannot precede this -ing form.","C":"She’s does not contract she was.","D":"She’s does not contract she does."}}},{"id":"c3639e14-b449-5772-a8f9-ca21c6b6195c","topicSlug":"register-variation","level":"C1","prompt":"Expand “she’d” in “She’d measure the garden fence if she had time.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"she had"},{"id":"B","text":"she did"},{"id":"C","text":"she should"},{"id":"D","text":"she would"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The following **base verb** and conditional result point to would.","explanation":"The base verb measure and hypothetical condition identify **she would**.","keywords":["expand-would-contraction"],"skill":"expand-would-contraction","contextKey":"register-variation-3","fingerprint":"419c47c55803c0515a002982cfd54c9776bcf3e02e25358f6e127ce098b9743b","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-varieties"],"version":"core-202