 verb unchanged.","B":"Would not changes the modal and meaning; it does not expand won’t.","C":"Will not takes an infinitive without to.","D":"The verb after will not must remain base form."}}},{"id":"85abc6f2-49ed-5057-aae4-6e0a8fb73e31","topicSlug":"register-variation","level":"C1","prompt":"Choose a standard polite modal request asking someone to measure the garden fence.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Could you to measure the garden fence, please?"},{"id":"B","text":"Could you measured the garden fence, please?"},{"id":"C","text":"Do could you measure the garden fence, please?"},{"id":"D","text":"Could you measure the garden fence, please?"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Use the **modal question** pattern to make a polite request.","explanation":"**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request.","keywords":["polite-request-register"],"skill":"polite-request-register","contextKey":"register-variation-3","fingerprint":"bf4996b8e63a8724cd8a534057b8a3521e31e6fda32aad2bee41d3d8532af03c","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-varieties"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Use the **modal question** pattern to make a polite request.","**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request.","Choose **Could you measure the garden fence, please?**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Could takes a bare infinitive without to.","B":"The main verb after could remains base, not past.","C":"Could forms its own question; do-support is not added.","D":"**Could you + base verb** is a standard polite request."}}},{"id":"f9a06cf6-df78-52bb-a1f7-21a6b8363f80","topicSlug":"register-variation","level":"C1","prompt":"Expand “she’s” in “She’s translating the travel leaflet right now.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"she has"},{"id":"B","text":"she was"},{"id":"C","text":"she does"},{"id":"D","text"